---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Chaos Front Guide"
  description="Learn how Chaos Front Guide verifies gameplay notes, records sources, and decides what is ready to publish."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="page-header stack">
        <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
        <h1>About Chaos Front Guide</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Chaos Front Guide is an English-first reference site for one game. It is built to answer
          player questions with observed results instead of generic game-catalog copy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-grid">
        <section class="article-copy stack">
          <h2>Publication policy</h2>
          <p>
            A guide must state the tested game build, the date of verification, the relevant source
            or original capture, the exact conclusion, and the conditions used to reach it.
          </p>
          <p>
            When a conclusion depends on a mission branch, a squad setup, a difficulty setting, or
            an unclear Demo limitation, the page will say so. Unsupported claims do not get a
            placeholder route or a search-optimized list page.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="article-copy stack">
          <h2>Source hierarchy</h2>
          <p>
            Repeatable in-game testing and original screenshots come first. Official store and
            developer material provide release context. Community reports may point to a test, but
            are not treated as confirmation on their own.
          </p>
          <p>
            The guide index expands only when enough evidence exists to maintain a useful, dated
            page. This keeps the site focused on Chaos Front rather than becoming a general game
            catalog.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
